Drive the visualiser in client-initiated mode too.

sendspin-visualizer-roles.diff attaches biscuit_sendspin_viz in
_handle_server_connection, which only runs when the server connects in. Since
r280 the daemon connects out to Music Assistant (--url), through
_run_client_initiated, which created its client without attaching it: music
played and the ring stayed dark. Attach it the same way, once, before the
client is used. The connection loop reuses this client across reconnects, so
once is enough.

Applied after sendspin-visualizer-roles.diff and sendspin-media-commands.diff,
and generated against a tree with both applied.

--- a/sendspin/daemon/daemon.py
+++ b/sendspin/daemon/daemon.py
@@ -209,6 +209,7 @@
         assert self._args.url is not None
         assert self._audio_handler is not None
         client = self._create_client()
+        biscuit_sendspin_viz.attach(client)
         self._server_url = self._args.url
         self._attach_client(client)
         await self._connection_loop(self._args.url)
